<title>JAPAN: Japan average rates on time deposits.</title>
<headline>Japan average rates on time deposits.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-10-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Average rates on time deposits of more than 10 million yen in the week to October 9 as released by the Bank of Japan on Wednesday:</p>
<p>    one mth	0.34 (0.35)	 one year     0.41 (0.41)</p>
<p>    three mths   0.35 (0.35)	 two years    0.56 (0.60)</p>
<p>    six mths     0.36 (0.36)	 three years  1.10 (1.15)</p>
<p>Average rates on time deposits of three to 10 million yen:</p>
<p>    one mth	0.30 (0.30)	 one year     0.36 (0.36)</p>
<p>    three mths   0.30 (0.30)	 two years    0.51 (0.55)</p>
<p>    six mths     0.31 (0.31)	 three years  1.06 (1.10)</p>
<p>Average rates on time deposits of less than three million</p>
<p>yen:</p>
<p>    one mth	0.25 (0.25)	 one year     0.32 (0.32)</p>
<p>    three mths   0.25 (0.25)	 two years    0.46 (0.49)</p>
<p>    six mths     0.26 (0.26)	 three years  1.01 (1.05)</p>
<p>Average rates on certificates of deposit, Oct 07 - Oct 11:</p>
<p>    less than 30 days  0.48 (0.50)   120-150 days  0.54 (0.54)</p>
<p>    30-60 days	   0.51 (0.52)   150-180 days  0.55 (0.55)</p>
<p>    60-90 days	   0.51 (0.52)   180-360 days  0.57 (0.59)</p>
<p>    90-120 days	  0.52 (0.53)   over 360 days 0.53 (1.28)</p>
